WEBVTT


00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.401
I wanna be a ballerina.
That's always been my dream.


00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:49.005
<i>My mom always said that I did</i>
<i>pirouettes before I even started walking.</i>


00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:53.083
And I did them and I fell on my butt.


00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.485
<i>I had a little ballerina on my nightstand,</i>


00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:01.048
and I think this was my first idea
why I wanted to become a ballerina,


00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:03.493
'cause I never knew that ballet existed.


00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.295
<i>I love hip-hop.</i>


00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:10.768
<i>Missy, Jay-Z, Common,</i>
<i>N.W.A., Kanye West.</i>


00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:15.637
Hip-hop allows you to let go
and follow the beat.


00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:21.776
<i>I think the biggest difference between</i>
<i>ballet and hip-hop is the posture.</i>


00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.414
<i>That settling into your body in hip-hop,</i>


00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.953
whereas ballet,
it's just about flying and flowing.


00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:32.114
I love kissing.
Stuffed pizza, are you kidding?


00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.586
Wrigley Field.


00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.662
Maybe dancing and kissing,
the same time.


00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:41.060
The lake, my friends and my dad.
Oh, my God, my dad, Roy...


00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.897
Trumpet. He's a trumpet player.
Trumpet.


00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:50.570
And this necklace. It's from my mom.
She gave it to me for luck.


00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.559
<i>It's not too much leaving home,</i>


00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.793
'cause I'm really excited
to go to New York,


00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.062
but it's the not knowing.


00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.567
Not knowing what's gonna happen,


00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.470
not knowing the people
who are gonna be in my life.


00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.919
My boyfriend and I decided
to see other people,


00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:47.056
because he's studying somewhere
and I'm here in New York,


00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.794
and it's probably better this way.


00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.426
My ankles are a little weak,


00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:53.199
and my turnout could be
probably a little better.


00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.105
Oh, it hurts so much.


00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:01.637
Don't you want me to do, like,
a pirouette or something?


00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.754
<i>This is what I've been doing</i>
<i>my whole life,</i>


00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.227
and honestly I don't think
I had time to do anything else,


00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.396
besides kissing.


00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.560
<i>I'm gonna be working really,</i>
<i>really hard to be the best.</i>


00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.831
<i>And you won't be disappointed in me.</i>


00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.736
<i>There are not gonna be</i>
<i>better dancers than me there.</i>


00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.901
<i>I'm going to be the best.</i>


00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:35.447
<i>And if there are,</i>
<i>they should just wait and see.</i>


00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.049
That's right.


00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.783
That's right.


00:03:58.238 --> 00:03:59.762
Hey, that was awesome.


00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.136
- What do you call that?
- An attitude.


00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.470
Oh, neat.


00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.875
- Are you Zoe?
- Uh-huh.


00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.537
I'm Sara.


00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:09.746
Yes, you'll do.


00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.846
Okay...


00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.510
You brought this
all the way from Texas?


00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:15.781
Yes.


00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:19.116
In Texas,
we have something called "gentlemen."


00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:22.092
I think I got something called a "hernia."


00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:25.029
How did you get it here
in the first place?


00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.597
Some horny cellist.


00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:31.226
Why don't we take some stuff out?
It will be easier to carry.


00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:34.568
Yes, that is an excellent idea.
Why didn't I think of that?


00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:41.103
Okay, that's my jewelry,
that's my top hat.


00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.573
That's Hamlet.


00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:56.022
I've always suspected
Ken was a serial killer.


00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.766
<i>Each of you has been blessed</i>
<i>with a unique gift.</i>


00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:09.072
- Trombone.
- What?


00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:12.167
I got this thing where I can look at
somebody, I can tell what they do.


00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:15.179
And you are a trombonista.


00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:19.311
Well, maybe your thing is broken,
'cause I'm here for ballet.


00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.683
What? You trying to be a ballerina?


00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:26.052
I am a ballerina.
I'm trying to become a prima ballerina.


00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.252
Well, you are kind of prima,
but you don't look like a ballerina.


00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.889
You've got the soul
of a trombone player.


00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.627
It's in the eyes.


00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:37.594
I...


00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:40.764
I'm Miles and you are...


00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:47.479
<i>From our ballet department,</i>
<i>Miss Monique Delacroix.</i>


00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:50.040
- You mind?
- I mind what?


00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:53.414
Turning that down.
I'm trying to hear Miss Delacroix.


00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:59.517
And by the way, the remix is way better.


00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:06.054
<i>Although I'm sure it's true</i>
<i>you're the best and brightest</i>


00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.691
<i>that your former schools</i>
<i>and teachers had to offer,</i>


00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:13.628
<i>I regret having to dash</i>
<i>your dreams of a meteoric rise</i>


00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:17.471
<i>to the pinnacle of artistic success</i>
<i>and world renown.</i>


00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.670
<i>By Juilliard choosing you,</i>


00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.030
<i>the bar's been raised.</i>


00:06:24.065 --> 00:06:25.179
<i>the bar's been raised.</i>


00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:31.016
<i>For the next four years,</i>
<i>you must strive for perfection.</i>


00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.993
<i>Please look to your left</i>


00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:38.720
<i>and your right.</i>


00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:46.633
<i>Only one in three of you</i>
<i>will go on to a life of fulfillment</i>


00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.240
<i>in the mastery of your art.</i>


00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:55.046
<i>The other two will probably end up</i>
<i>stocking books at Barnes & Noble</i>


00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:58.706
<i>or working behind a cosmetic counter</i>
<i>in Buffalo.</i>


00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.554
<i>Welcome to Juilliard.</i>


00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:09.316
Thanks.


00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:12.956
Oh, my God!
How pretentious can you get?


00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:17.161
I mean, I know she's your idol, you have
the poster over the bed and all but...


00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.465
Monique Delacroix has danced the lead


00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.631
with every major ballet company
in the world.


00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.038
She was a principal


00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:25.372
at the American Ballet Theatre
for 15 years.


00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:27.207
- Whatever.
- What?


00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:30.282
You wanna wind up working
in a cosmetics counter in Buffalo?


00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:31.782
The women in my family don't work.


00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:34.546
They drink martinis,
and they get face-lifts.


00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:36.645
Me, I just wanna act


00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:40.556
and leave the world domination
to you and Mistress Delacroix.


00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:45.289
Oh, my God. There's my mentor.


00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.866
He's beautiful. I hate him.


00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.959
I better go and pay my respects.
See you.


00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.681
- Hi.
- Hello.


00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:14.017
Hi. I'm Sara, your mentee.


00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:18.355
Well, sit down
before that tray tips you over.


00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:25.601
- So, Sara, you any good?
- Yes. But isn't everybody?


00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:28.336
We wouldn't be here if we weren't.


00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.144
See you.


00:08:39.085 --> 00:08:40.746
- Bye.
- Okay.


00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:44.020
I'll watch out for you as best I can.


00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:48.282
But for the most part,
you're on your own.


00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:52.157
So we're all
totally freaking wasted, right?


00:08:52.265 --> 00:08:54.756
And guess
who gets on the freaking elevator?


00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:57.927
- Do you pluck your eyebrows?
- What?


00:08:58.571 --> 00:09:01.131
Your eyebrows,
where do you get them done?


00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:05.871
Round the corner on 9th,
at the Chinese place.


00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:06.967
Cool.


00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:11.140
Never ever date an actor.
All they wanna do is screw ballerinas.


00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.410
It's like a fetish.


00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:15.578
Besides, when you dump them,
they're such drama queens.


00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:19.282
So do you have a boyfriend?


00:09:20.126 --> 00:09:22.094
Yes. Well, no.


00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:25.128
He's in premed at Georgetown,
and I'm here.


00:09:25.298 --> 00:09:27.061
We decided we could date
other people...


00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:29.964
Forget about him. It's for the best.


00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:32.635
Honestly, there's
maybe seven ballet companies


00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:34.205
worth dancing for in the world.


00:09:34.307 --> 00:09:36.468
That means you have to stay focused.


00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:38.839
Boyfriends, they just get in the way.


00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:54.018
My God, this summer in Paris,
I was like the ugly American


00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:56.890
because my sissonne ouverte
wasn't <i>grande</i> enough.


00:09:58.264 --> 00:10:00.357
Who'd you take class with?


00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:02.491
- Me?
- Yes, you.


00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:05.296
The Chicago Ballet with Uri Pell.


00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:08.805
Oh, I know him. He's kind of out there.


00:10:09.342 --> 00:10:11.970
If you mean progressive,
yeah, he's kind of out there.


00:10:12.078 --> 00:10:15.514
He did the thing where everybody
was like keys on a typewriter.


00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:17.715
Were you in that?


00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:20.411
Sara, come with me for a moment.


00:10:25.424 --> 00:10:28.018
- Stand here.
- Why?


00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.501
- What's your name?
- Sara.


00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:47.073
Sara Johnson.


00:10:49.248 --> 00:10:53.742
You'd all do well to follow
Miss Johnson's example.


00:10:54.687 --> 00:10:57.053
Class begins at 9:30 sharp,


00:10:57.156 --> 00:11:02.719
which means that 9:29 you should all
be stretched and waiting for my arrival.


00:11:18.244 --> 00:11:20.610
And you, what's your name?


00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.907
- Marcus.
- Marcus, what is this place?


00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:30.546
- A dance studio?
- No, it's a cathedral.


00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:35.817
In this room dwells the entire
spiritual history of our species.


00:11:36.662 --> 00:11:39.426
How can you hope
to be part of that, Marcus,


00:11:39.565 --> 00:11:43.899
while wearing trousers that go "whish,
whish" every time you take a step?


00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.297
- I...
- You can't.


00:11:47.239 --> 00:11:51.573
Not one article of vinyl clothing
is to cross that threshold.


00:11:52.912 --> 00:11:55.210
- Are we clear?
- Yes.


00:11:57.116 --> 00:11:58.140
- Morning, Bella.
- Morning.


00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.239
Morning.


00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:07.421
You will be divided into three lines
based on your abilities.


00:12:09.562 --> 00:12:11.860
We will do this in every class.


00:12:13.733 --> 00:12:17.897
If you find yourself in line number three
more than five weeks,


00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:21.537
you will be asked to leave the program.


00:12:24.677 --> 00:12:26.941
Please line up at the long bar.


00:12:27.513 --> 00:12:28.980
Marcus,


00:12:30.216 --> 00:12:31.513
third line.


00:12:31.684 --> 00:12:33.845
Bella. Please.


00:12:34.553 --> 00:12:37.386
We'll begin with pliés.


00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:47.596
What happened to your eye?


00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.760
I was in circus class, I fell off my stilts.


00:12:51.904 --> 00:12:55.032
Is that something you should be doing
on a first day?


00:12:55.274 --> 00:12:58.607
Welcome to
Introduction to Hip-Hop Theory.


00:12:59.211 --> 00:12:59.741
Oh, my God.


00:12:59.776 --> 00:13:00.271
Oh, my God.


00:13:00.379 --> 00:13:03.246
What? You're the one
who made us take this class.


00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:07.844
My name is Miles Sultana,
and I am not your professor.


00:13:08.687 --> 00:13:12.555
Your actual professor was trying to ball
with us young bucks up in the Bronx,


00:13:12.658 --> 00:13:15.149
decided to go all half-man,
half-amazing to the hole.


00:13:15.261 --> 00:13:18.560
Needless to say he pulled his hammy.
I laughed 'cause it was funny


00:13:18.664 --> 00:13:20.063
until he fell to the ground,


00:13:20.166 --> 00:13:22.430
and his leg bent backwards
and snapped in three places.


00:13:22.535 --> 00:13:24.230
This school is dangerous.


00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:29.403
So here I am filling in for him until he...
Well, if he gets back.


00:13:29.708 --> 00:13:33.940
So with the help of my good friend
Franz here and his instrument,


00:13:34.046 --> 00:13:37.777
we are going to explore
the nature of hip-hop within us all.


00:13:39.318 --> 00:13:42.776
All right. So, hip-hop theory.


00:13:43.689 --> 00:13:45.281
What is hip-hop?


00:13:48.794 --> 00:13:51.228
Ah, Trombonista.


00:13:54.533 --> 00:13:56.091
<i>Hip-hop is the convergence</i>


00:13:56.202 --> 00:13:59.035
<i>of the electronic musical movement</i>
<i>and urban youth culture</i>


00:13:59.138 --> 00:14:02.403
<i>which happened after the world</i>
<i>discovered that disco sucked.</i>


00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:07.111
Good answer.
I ain't giving up my Bee Gees.


00:14:08.214 --> 00:14:09.306
<i>Hip-hop is...</i>


00:14:09.415 --> 00:14:10.507
- It's rap.
<i>- You know what I'm saying?</i>


00:14:10.616 --> 00:14:11.640
<i>Hip-hop is...</i>


00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:12.739
Soul.


00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:13.841
<i>Hip-hop is...</i>


00:14:13.953 --> 00:14:14.977
R & B.


00:14:15.087 --> 00:14:16.054
<i>Hip-hop is...</i>


00:14:16.155 --> 00:14:19.556
Funk. For most people today,
hip-hop is about bling-bling.


00:14:19.658 --> 00:14:21.717
But what was before the bling-bling?


00:14:21.827 --> 00:14:25.729
What was before the Escalades,
and the nine millys and the hoochies?


00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:33.839
<i>Hip-hop is...</i>


00:14:33.939 --> 00:14:35.406
It's a form
of cross-cultural communication.


00:14:35.507 --> 00:14:38.067
<i>- Hip-hop is...</i>
- It's a lifestyle, a language, a fashion.


00:14:38.177 --> 00:14:40.008
<i>- Hip-hip is...</i>
- It's simple and complex.


00:14:40.112 --> 00:14:43.013
It's about a individual
questioning the establishment.


00:14:43.115 --> 00:14:46.482
It's about recombining, combining
everything that came before.


00:14:47.253 --> 00:14:49.551
Hip-hop is about finding a new voice.


00:14:49.655 --> 00:14:53.284
But what hip-hop really is can be
summed up in three simple words.


00:14:53.559 --> 00:14:55.652
I am here.


00:15:00.532 --> 00:15:02.261
It was so rad


00:15:02.368 --> 00:15:04.359
the way you like looped
my roomie's words,


00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:06.097
then you made a song out of it.


00:15:06.205 --> 00:15:09.299
Thanks.
So did your roomie think so, too?


00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:11.000
You could have told me
you were a teacher.


00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.806
- I'm not.
- Okay, a guest lecturer then.


00:15:14.013 --> 00:15:16.607
- I thought you were an actor.
- An actor. Why?


00:15:17.249 --> 00:15:18.546
Never mind.


00:15:18.751 --> 00:15:20.378
How tall are you?


00:15:21.253 --> 00:15:24.279
- 5'10".
- You wanna wrestle?


00:15:25.524 --> 00:15:27.389
Okay, let's go.


00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.193
Hey, you guys should come
to the club I'm spinning at tonight.


00:15:31.297 --> 00:15:33.822
I have a class in the morning.


00:15:33.933 --> 00:15:37.869
I can put you two on the list, plus one
so you can bring your boyfriend.


00:15:38.037 --> 00:15:39.732
I don't have a boyfriend.


00:15:41.473 --> 00:15:45.432
All right, cool.
So just the two of you then.


00:15:50.149 --> 00:15:52.515
- We'll see.
- Cool.


00:15:57.122 --> 00:15:58.646
Zoe.


00:15:59.391 --> 00:16:01.951
5'11" actually, with shoes.


00:16:16.175 --> 00:16:17.938
Second line.


00:16:26.151 --> 00:16:27.880
Second line.


00:16:31.223 --> 00:16:32.850
Line one.


00:16:38.797 --> 00:16:41.061
What is that?


00:16:42.901 --> 00:16:44.994
It felt more natural that way.


00:16:45.337 --> 00:16:48.568
You're not here to be natural.
You're here to learn ballet.


00:16:53.379 --> 00:16:55.108
Second line.


00:16:58.117 --> 00:17:00.608
Must be all that fine Chicago training.


00:17:12.898 --> 00:17:16.163
Wow. Well, look at this place, momma.


00:17:16.268 --> 00:17:18.998
Only a few minutes in New York
and already we're on the list


00:17:19.104 --> 00:17:21.038
at the hottest spot in town.


00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.906
- Okay. Momma?
- Okay, I'm exploring my range.


00:17:25.878 --> 00:17:28.176
- "Momma" is not in my range?
- No.


00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.172
- Hey.
- Hi.


00:17:30.416 --> 00:17:32.008
- Hi.
- Let's go.


00:17:32.251 --> 00:17:34.378
Okay, remember,
we can't stay up too late.


00:17:34.486 --> 00:17:36.113
I know, I know. Hey, chill, momma.


00:17:36.221 --> 00:17:39.384
- Jeez! Ballerinas.
- I don't really... None of...


00:17:39.491 --> 00:17:41.857
- I don't really dance.
- Hey.


00:17:42.027 --> 00:17:44.359
- I knew you'd come.
- Hi.


00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:47.528
- Who's this?
- Hello to you, too.


00:17:47.633 --> 00:17:49.999
- Sara, Candy.
- Nice to meet you.


00:17:50.569 --> 00:17:53.231
- I'm sure it is.
- Okay...


00:17:53.338 --> 00:17:55.363
Hey, don't mind her.
She's like that with everybody.


00:17:55.474 --> 00:17:56.634
Come on.


00:17:56.775 --> 00:17:58.766
What about my drink?


00:17:59.812 --> 00:18:01.643
- Where are we going?
- To the pit.


00:18:01.747 --> 00:18:02.839
Pit?


00:18:20.499 --> 00:18:24.265
Wow! This is a whole other level.


00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:27.161
Yeah, I used to have to sneak out


00:18:27.272 --> 00:18:31.038
and take the 9 train up to
the South Bronx to see stuff like this.


00:18:32.711 --> 00:18:34.804
It's funny, 'cause most of these kids,


00:18:34.913 --> 00:18:37.848
they don't even realize
that there's a history there,


00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:39.744
a shadow behind every move.


00:18:39.852 --> 00:18:43.310
Every step they make
is into a footprint bigger than their own.


00:18:47.292 --> 00:18:48.816
Kind of like ballet.


00:18:51.663 --> 00:18:53.096
Professor!


00:18:54.666 --> 00:18:57.567
I'm paying you to spin,
not stand still, man.


00:18:58.504 --> 00:19:01.371
This is Mixx,
he's the father of this party.


00:19:01.473 --> 00:19:04.636
- And who is this pretty distraction?
- This is Sara.


00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:08.407
- She's one of my students.
- Should have stayed in school.


00:19:09.014 --> 00:19:11.039
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you, too.


00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:13.015
Yes, yes, yes, yes.


00:19:13.785 --> 00:19:16.185
- That's my girl, Candy.
- Yeah, we've met.


00:19:16.288 --> 00:19:18.222
It don't get much flyer than Candy.


00:19:18.323 --> 00:19:19.449
Anything she do, you can bet,


00:19:19.558 --> 00:19:22.322
next week,
see 100 kids doing the same thing.


00:19:22.427 --> 00:19:24.622
- Or at least trying.
- Know what I'm saying, right?


00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:27.164
Yo, honor and pleasure to meet you,
little lady.


00:19:27.266 --> 00:19:29.234
I have to go be the man.
Y'all enjoy the party.


00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:32.201
You, over here wasting my money,
go do your thing tonight, man.


00:19:32.304 --> 00:19:34.295
- All right, man.
- All right, man.


00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:37.538
- I got to go spin. Straight?
- Yeah.


00:19:37.643 --> 00:19:38.735
- You sure?
- Yeah.


00:19:38.844 --> 00:19:41.870
- You're not scared?
- You ever audition for Juilliard?


00:19:43.749 --> 00:19:48.345
We gonna heat it up for you.
That's in case you decide to go in.


00:20:05.704 --> 00:20:08.104
<i>Yo, what's going on?</i>
<i>This is your boy, Daddy Mix.</i>


00:20:08.207 --> 00:20:10.698
<i>Hey, I'm about to bring my man</i>
<i>out on the ones and twos right now.</i>


00:20:10.809 --> 00:20:12.276
<i>But we gonna have to bring him out</i>
<i>the right way.</i>


00:20:12.377 --> 00:20:13.674
<i>I'm gonna need y'all to repeat after me.</i>


00:20:13.779 --> 00:20:15.804
<i>We gonna do it like this. Yo! Say,</i>


00:20:15.914 --> 00:20:18.280
<i>Hey, one, two, check it out</i>


00:20:18.383 --> 00:20:20.578
<i>Hey, one, two, check it out</i>


00:20:20.686 --> 00:20:22.881
<i>Hey, one, two, check it out</i>


00:20:22.988 --> 00:20:25.821
<i>Hey, one, two, check it out</i>


00:20:25.924 --> 00:20:27.858
<i>Do your thing, boy</i>


00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:30.724
<i>Yo, this is your boy, Mike L-E-S.</i>


00:20:30.829 --> 00:20:33.923
<i>Yo, big show tonight.</i>
<i>Time for wylin' out Chi-town style.</i>


00:20:34.032 --> 00:20:36.057
<i>Y'all know what to do.</i>


00:21:04.496 --> 00:21:06.259
So what are you waiting for?


00:21:17.276 --> 00:21:18.937
Come on, girl!


00:21:29.588 --> 00:21:31.419
What's up? Can you take it?


00:22:16.501 --> 00:22:17.661
Yeah.


00:22:33.385 --> 00:22:34.852
She's really good!


00:23:21.266 --> 00:23:22.790
Oh, my God!


00:23:57.903 --> 00:24:00.895
- What was that?
- Dude, that was awesome!


00:24:01.006 --> 00:24:02.439
What?


00:24:05.177 --> 00:24:08.203
- That's not water.
- I know. It's vodka.


00:24:29.501 --> 00:24:31.731
Hey, Sara.
Hey, yo, I'm sorry I couldn't get back.


00:24:31.837 --> 00:24:35.637
This other kid was supposed to spin,
but he didn't show. But, yo...


00:24:35.774 --> 00:24:37.833
I saw you killing them in the pit all night.


00:24:37.943 --> 00:24:41.003
- What? You were amazing.
- Thank you.


00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:43.205
You weren't too bad yourself.


00:24:43.949 --> 00:24:47.942
We were gonna go get some breakfast
if you wanted to...


00:24:48.053 --> 00:24:51.284
I can't. I've got class in, like,
three-and-a-half hours.


00:24:58.129 --> 00:25:00.597
Looks like Franz found a friend.


00:25:02.601 --> 00:25:03.932
Oh...


00:25:05.036 --> 00:25:08.631
I should probably get my roommate
home before she hurts somebody.


00:25:15.046 --> 00:25:16.343
Okay, see you.


00:25:20.986 --> 00:25:23.216
Okay, let's go.


00:25:26.424 --> 00:25:28.517
- Okay.
- See ya.


00:26:20.946 --> 00:26:22.072
No...


00:26:22.180 --> 00:26:24.375
- Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
- What?


00:26:33.858 --> 00:26:35.621
Allegro.


00:26:35.727 --> 00:26:37.251
Please wake up.


00:26:37.662 --> 00:26:39.687
You're thinking too much.


00:26:40.765 --> 00:26:42.528
It's not your job.


00:26:42.901 --> 00:26:46.496
Thought was put into these steps
hundreds of years ago.


00:26:47.272 --> 00:26:51.675
It's simply your duty to execute it
as it was handed down.


00:26:51.776 --> 00:26:53.266
Faster.


00:26:57.148 --> 00:26:58.410
Stop.


00:26:59.250 --> 00:27:00.717
What are you doing?


00:27:01.386 --> 00:27:04.082
- I'm sorry, Miss Delacroix.
- You what?


00:27:06.358 --> 00:27:07.916
I'm sorry.


00:27:11.196 --> 00:27:12.754
Look at me.


00:27:16.067 --> 00:27:17.625
You smell of alcohol.


00:27:18.803 --> 00:27:21.294
Did you need a drink
to prepare for class?


00:27:22.273 --> 00:27:25.174
- No.
- Then why do you smell like a tavern?


00:27:26.144 --> 00:27:28.112
I went out with some friends.


00:27:28.546 --> 00:27:30.138
Oh, did you now?


00:27:30.448 --> 00:27:32.439
Where did your friends take you?


00:27:34.285 --> 00:27:36.981
- To a club.
- To a club?


00:27:37.989 --> 00:27:39.650
Was it a ballet club?


00:27:42.694 --> 00:27:43.956
No.


00:27:47.365 --> 00:27:49.833
Do you know
what's behind the third line?


00:27:53.271 --> 00:27:56.172
Nothing.
There's nothing behind the third line.


00:27:57.442 --> 00:28:00.639
That nothing's a... It's a magical place
where you can eat what you want,


00:28:00.745 --> 00:28:03.908
and you can sleep in
and have ice cream


00:28:04.382 --> 00:28:06.350
and cheeseburgers and candy and...


00:28:06.451 --> 00:28:09.443
And you can...
And you can wear what you want.


00:28:09.554 --> 00:28:12.648
And you can drink whenever you like,
and then you can come in here,


00:28:12.757 --> 00:28:16.454
and you can pretend that there are
no consequences to your actions.


00:28:16.561 --> 00:28:20.395
But that nothing
does not reside within these walls.


00:28:25.103 --> 00:28:26.730
Third line.


00:28:30.508 --> 00:28:31.702
Bella.


00:29:04.509 --> 00:29:07.444
<i>"I've often been asked</i>
<i>what is the key to my success.</i>


00:29:08.046 --> 00:29:10.537
<i>"The answer is always the same.</i>


00:29:11.282 --> 00:29:15.685
<i>"I have never allowed anyone</i>
<i>to stand in the way of my heart."</i>


00:29:18.556 --> 00:29:20.023
What did I do?


00:29:20.125 --> 00:29:22.093
- I don't know. What did you do?
- I don't know.


00:29:22.193 --> 00:29:25.219
You just been jetting out of here
every day like you stole something.


00:29:25.330 --> 00:29:26.558
See you.


00:29:26.831 --> 00:29:30.028
I need to spend more time practicing,
get focused.


00:29:30.568 --> 00:29:31.967
Well, I know this place
around the corner.


00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:33.901
Best cannolis on the Upper West Side.
Maybe we could...


00:29:34.005 --> 00:29:35.563
I really don't have time to go anywhere.


00:29:35.673 --> 00:29:37.834
So I got these friends
that own a art gallery downtown,


00:29:37.942 --> 00:29:39.500
and they're doing this big show
on street art.


00:29:39.611 --> 00:29:42.045
Graffiti, tag and all the way
from the beginning till now.


00:29:42.147 --> 00:29:44.945
They asked this guy Nigel,
who's a video director,


00:29:45.049 --> 00:29:46.710
real creative cat, to pull together


00:29:46.818 --> 00:29:49.548
a video installation/performance piece
for the exhibit.


00:29:49.654 --> 00:29:51.144
And he asked me to handle the music,


00:29:51.256 --> 00:29:54.089
and I was hoping that maybe
you could help me out.


00:29:54.526 --> 00:29:56.756
- How?
- Choreograph a dance piece.


00:29:57.162 --> 00:29:58.993
- Me?
- Yeah, you.


00:29:59.264 --> 00:30:00.390
Why me?


00:30:00.498 --> 00:30:04.628
What you did back at the club, that was
some of the illest stuff I've ever seen.


00:30:06.571 --> 00:30:08.198
Look, I'd love to help you out.


00:30:08.306 --> 00:30:11.207
But I'm doing everything I can
just to keep my head above water...


00:30:11.309 --> 00:30:13.573
- Sara.
...in my classes, okay?


00:30:15.079 --> 00:30:17.172
- I'm sorry.
- Hey.


00:30:18.583 --> 00:30:20.483
- What's this?
- Just some beats I been working on.


00:30:20.585 --> 00:30:21.950
It's kind of off the bubble.


00:30:22.053 --> 00:30:25.716
None of that Hot 97 rah-rah.
You know what I'm saying?


00:30:26.024 --> 00:30:27.582
Just listen to it.


00:30:37.435 --> 00:30:39.096
Was that you humming just now?


00:30:39.204 --> 00:30:41.832
It's beatboxing. It's humming 2.0.


00:30:42.407 --> 00:30:44.739
- It's odd.
- It's part of my culture.


00:30:44.843 --> 00:30:47.710
That's not what I meant. What I meant,


00:30:49.013 --> 00:30:50.810
that most people
wouldn't be able to revisit


00:30:50.915 --> 00:30:52.678
the site of their greatest failure


00:30:52.784 --> 00:30:54.274
with so much ease.


00:30:55.753 --> 00:30:59.780
What is it about you that
makes you so comfortable with defeat?


00:31:00.792 --> 00:31:02.225
You seem pretty relaxed.


00:31:02.327 --> 00:31:04.090
What was the last dancer
you got into ABT?


00:31:04.195 --> 00:31:05.787
San Francisco? Joffrey?


00:31:07.932 --> 00:31:10.162
- Losing your touch, huh?
- No.


00:31:10.635 --> 00:31:12.728
I'm just maintaining my standards.


00:31:30.588 --> 00:31:31.919
Morning, Bella.


00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:44.295
I can't even get out of the third line.


00:31:44.402 --> 00:31:46.370
She's making an example of you.


00:31:46.838 --> 00:31:47.896
Lucky me.


00:31:48.006 --> 00:31:50.839
I'm, like, this close from Monique
presenting me as her protégé.


00:31:52.277 --> 00:31:53.539
Oh, my God.


00:31:54.245 --> 00:31:56.372
I've never been so sore in my life.


00:31:57.181 --> 00:31:58.443
Get used to it.


00:31:58.750 --> 00:32:01.810
I don't think I've slept
more than four hours since I got here.


00:32:01.920 --> 00:32:04.115
If there's one thing in life
I could get rid of, it'd be sleep.


00:32:04.222 --> 00:32:05.917
It's such a waste of time.


00:32:06.190 --> 00:32:07.919
Such a waste.


00:32:14.732 --> 00:32:16.063
I don't do drugs.


00:32:16.734 --> 00:32:18.463
It's not heroin, Sara.


00:32:20.838 --> 00:32:22.066
Just remember,


00:32:22.874 --> 00:32:25.775
Xenical is your pal
when you want to keep the weight off.


00:32:25.877 --> 00:32:28.641
Percocet's best for the knees
that want to fall off.


00:32:29.380 --> 00:32:33.544
And Ambien is your friend
when you just need to doze off.


00:32:40.959 --> 00:32:43.484
You want to get out of the third line,
don't you?


00:32:48.833 --> 00:32:50.630
I don't want to be
the goddamn quirky brunette.


00:32:50.735 --> 00:32:52.965
- What?
- Every play I've ever been in,


00:32:53.137 --> 00:32:56.868
I wind up playing this witty-yet-lovable,
slightly insane girl


00:32:56.975 --> 00:32:59.205
with the plaid skirt and weird laugh.


00:33:00.044 --> 00:33:01.875
Yeah, you're right.
That doesn't sound like you at all.


00:33:01.980 --> 00:33:03.345
So we're doing this play,


00:33:03.448 --> 00:33:06.975
and the lead character is this quirky,
well, homicidal brunette type,


00:33:07.085 --> 00:33:08.814
and of course
they want me to read for it.


00:33:08.920 --> 00:33:11.184
- Wow, the lead. That's great.
- No, that's not great.


00:33:11.289 --> 00:33:15.692
Jeez, are you even listening to me?
If I do this now, it will never stop.


00:33:15.960 --> 00:33:19.487
That'll be it for me. I'll always be
the goddamn quirky brunette.


00:33:19.597 --> 00:33:22.566
- Then don't do it.
- No. I can't not do it.


00:33:22.667 --> 00:33:25.431
This could be my big break.
I could get an agent.


00:33:26.237 --> 00:33:28.728
So why don't you just read
for another part?


00:34:05.443 --> 00:34:07.001
I'm not gonna quit


00:34:07.812 --> 00:34:09.439
no matter how hard you push me,


00:34:09.547 --> 00:34:12.914
or how much you single me out
as an example of what not to do.


00:34:13.051 --> 00:34:14.780
I worked too hard to get here.


00:34:14.886 --> 00:34:18.151
And I am prepared
to do whatever it takes to be the best.


00:34:19.157 --> 00:34:22.285
You're gonna have to pack my bags
if you want me gone.


00:34:25.296 --> 00:34:28.026
- Are you done, Sara?
- Yes.


00:34:46.918 --> 00:34:48.510
- So...
- Jesus!


00:34:48.619 --> 00:34:50.143
Sure you don't want to get a cannoli?


00:34:50.254 --> 00:34:51.881
I'm doing some research.


00:34:53.858 --> 00:34:55.758
Trying to get inside
the master's head, huh?


00:34:55.860 --> 00:34:57.760
But I hear it's a scary place.


00:34:58.362 --> 00:35:01.525
You seem to know a lot
about this school for a guest lecturer.


00:35:01.632 --> 00:35:03.896
Well, that's 'cause I used to go here.


00:35:05.403 --> 00:35:07.337
- What?
- You heard me.


00:35:07.705 --> 00:35:08.933
You went here?


00:35:09.140 --> 00:35:12.371
Hey, I may not look like it,
but I'm a pretty cultured cat.


00:35:12.643 --> 00:35:16.238
- What were you here for?
- Piano. Composition actually.


00:35:18.349 --> 00:35:20.613
- You must've been good.
- Damn straight.


00:35:20.885 --> 00:35:23.012
- So I dropped out.
- What?


00:35:24.455 --> 00:35:26.218
Why would you give this up?


00:35:27.592 --> 00:35:28.616
It just wasn't for me.


00:35:28.726 --> 00:35:31.490
So did you listen
to those tracks I gave you?


00:35:31.596 --> 00:35:33.029
Look, you're gonna have
to get somebody else.


00:35:33.131 --> 00:35:36.760
- I don't want anybody else. I want you.
- You don't even know me.


00:35:36.868 --> 00:35:38.995
I know what I saw at the club that night.


00:35:39.103 --> 00:35:41.003
- Get Candy to choreograph it.
- Forget Candy.


00:35:41.105 --> 00:35:43.903
Nigel said it'll take one day.
We can shoot this weekend.


00:35:44.008 --> 00:35:45.703
- This weekend?
- It'll be fun.


00:35:45.810 --> 00:35:47.437
I'm not here for fun.


00:35:49.347 --> 00:35:51.508
<i>This Sara Johnson,</i>
<i>what do we know about her?</i>


00:35:51.616 --> 00:35:53.846
Well, she studied
at a few small princess academies


00:35:53.951 --> 00:35:55.919
and then last year with Uri Pell.


00:35:56.287 --> 00:35:59.120
Her father's a musician.
I've never heard of him, though.


00:35:59.223 --> 00:36:01.953
- And her mother?
- She died last year.


00:36:02.059 --> 00:36:05.586
Actually, around the same time
she first auditioned for Juilliard.


00:36:05.696 --> 00:36:07.664
I read her file. I'm her mentor.


00:36:10.468 --> 00:36:11.958
- Here you go.
- Thanks.


00:36:17.708 --> 00:36:18.834
Here you go.


00:36:19.610 --> 00:36:21.305
Monique wants to see you.


00:36:23.080 --> 00:36:26.311
- You feeling okay?
- Yeah. I'm just a little tired.


00:36:35.523 --> 00:36:38.185
- Marcus, are you okay?
- I just had my review.


00:36:39.260 --> 00:36:40.522
She dropped me.


00:36:41.328 --> 00:36:44.559
She made me work my ass off.
How can I just go home?


00:36:46.333 --> 00:36:47.561
I'm sorry.


00:37:00.014 --> 00:37:01.276
Close the door.


00:37:03.918 --> 00:37:05.010
Come.


00:37:09.957 --> 00:37:12.755
I've observed some things
that are distressing me.


00:37:12.993 --> 00:37:16.360
You need to work on your turnout.
Your arms are overly expressive.


00:37:16.464 --> 00:37:17.897
You keep turning...


00:37:18.199 --> 00:37:19.223
Sara?


00:37:19.333 --> 00:37:21.767
- I think I'm going to be sick.
- Oh, my God.


00:37:28.743 --> 00:37:31.541
Kleenex. Kleenex. Kleenex.


00:37:36.383 --> 00:37:37.714
Here you go.


00:37:40.821 --> 00:37:44.257
- I'm sorry.
- No. It's all right. Are you all right now?


00:37:45.192 --> 00:37:47.251
- Can I take it?
- Yes.


00:37:48.729 --> 00:37:49.821
Oh, God.


00:37:53.934 --> 00:37:55.401
You're taking pills.


00:38:01.742 --> 00:38:03.607
I've never taken them before.


00:38:04.545 --> 00:38:07.412
I swear. Just, my body hurts.


00:38:07.648 --> 00:38:10.344
I can't sleep, can't eat.


00:38:11.852 --> 00:38:13.911
I just... I don't know what to do,


00:38:14.755 --> 00:38:17.087
and this is the first time it happened.


00:38:23.531 --> 00:38:24.793
It's just hard.


00:38:28.202 --> 00:38:31.968
Sara, it's supposed to be hard.
It wouldn't be worth it if it weren't.


00:38:41.415 --> 00:38:42.905
Now we have to focus


00:38:44.785 --> 00:38:47.015
on strengthening your ankles.


00:38:48.622 --> 00:38:49.987
I'm not being cut?


00:38:51.058 --> 00:38:52.753
Why would you think that?


00:40:07.368 --> 00:40:08.528
Very good.


00:40:09.570 --> 00:40:12.038
Please clear the studio
for the next class.


00:40:19.046 --> 00:40:21.446
- How did I do?
- You were brilliant.


00:40:21.916 --> 00:40:23.611
But I'm not your frigging cheerleader,
so in the future,


00:40:23.717 --> 00:40:25.651
if you're curious about
your performance, look in the mirror.


00:40:25.753 --> 00:40:27.653
That's what they're there for.


00:40:50.945 --> 00:40:53.709
I was pretty surprised you found time
to fit me and my cannoli in.


00:40:53.814 --> 00:40:56.806
Well, it kind of threw me there.
That whole Juilliard drop-out thing.


00:40:56.917 --> 00:41:00.444
- Why didn't you tell me earlier?
- Dunno. It never came up.


00:41:00.821 --> 00:41:02.755
Guess I was being a little harsh.


00:41:02.856 --> 00:41:06.451
You have no idea how intimidating
Monique Delacroix can be.


00:41:07.661 --> 00:41:10.824
- Listen, Sara, about that...
- No. It wasn't you. I'm sorry.


00:41:12.132 --> 00:41:15.863
I just didn't realize how intense
Juilliard would really be, you know?


00:41:16.537 --> 00:41:18.198
It's so important to me.


00:41:19.640 --> 00:41:20.698
Why?


00:41:21.709 --> 00:41:22.801
Since I was little,


00:41:22.910 --> 00:41:26.676
my mom and I always dreamed about
me becoming a famous ballerina.


00:41:27.715 --> 00:41:29.148
The day of my


00:41:29.817 --> 00:41:33.048
first audition for Juilliard,
she really wanted to be there.


00:41:33.354 --> 00:41:35.345
I really wanted her to be there.


00:41:36.690 --> 00:41:38.351
It was my turn to dance.


00:41:39.159 --> 00:41:41.252
So I looked around,


00:41:43.030 --> 00:41:44.793
and I knew something was wrong.


00:41:45.599 --> 00:41:49.592
I was right. She died in a car accident
trying to get to my audition.


00:41:55.409 --> 00:41:56.501
Here.


00:42:01.048 --> 00:42:02.777
- What about you?
- Me?


00:42:03.350 --> 00:42:04.942
I was raised by wolves.


00:42:06.887 --> 00:42:09.651
And are you
and your wolf parents close?


00:42:10.624 --> 00:42:14.924
My mom and dad split when I was three.
I lived with my grandfather till he died,


00:42:15.329 --> 00:42:16.887
and then I went to school.


00:42:18.098 --> 00:42:20.464
Now I'm on my own, struggling, striving.


00:42:22.069 --> 00:42:23.400
Do you miss him?


00:42:24.638 --> 00:42:26.162
Yeah. He was wild.


00:42:26.707 --> 00:42:30.234
Mad old-school but a real cool cat.
He bought me my first record.


00:42:30.344 --> 00:42:33.802
Speaking of which,
did you listen to that CD I gave you?


00:42:35.049 --> 00:42:36.573
- I did.
- Really?


00:42:37.451 --> 00:42:39.885
It's hot. You got promise.


00:42:41.889 --> 00:42:46.053
Okay. So, what's it gonna take
for Sara Johnson to help me out?


00:42:50.197 --> 00:42:53.826
- You are not gonna make me beg.
- Yes. Yes, I am.


00:42:55.302 --> 00:42:58.794
Sara, please help me do this.


00:43:02.109 --> 00:43:03.804
- It's just one day, right?
- Just one day.


00:43:03.911 --> 00:43:08.041
And there will absolutely be no fun
involved at all, guaranteed.


00:43:14.621 --> 00:43:15.918
I'll think about it.


00:43:17.124 --> 00:43:18.250
You'll think... What?


00:43:18.358 --> 00:43:20.656
What're you talking about,
you'll think about it?


00:43:31.305 --> 00:43:35.264
Class, I'm sure you're all waiting
to hear about the fall production.


00:43:35.375 --> 00:43:38.606
This year, we'll be dancing
the classic romance, <i>Giselle.</i>


00:43:39.313 --> 00:43:41.747
I recommend
that you all study it closely.


00:43:42.149 --> 00:43:45.915
<i>Giselle</i> is possibly
one of the greatest works in the canon.


00:43:46.086 --> 00:43:49.021
<i>Giselle</i> requires
uncommon technical virtuosity.


00:43:49.289 --> 00:43:51.450
Its beauty is uncompromising.


00:43:51.592 --> 00:43:55.153
And I shall be equally uncompromising
in my choices.


00:43:55.262 --> 00:43:58.720
All the roles are open. Class dismissed.


00:44:06.673 --> 00:44:10.541
What a bitch! She's a jealous bitch.


00:44:10.644 --> 00:44:13.875
Katrina is, like, this close to being
presented as Monique's protégé.


00:44:13.981 --> 00:44:16.040
She has no reason to be jealous.


00:44:16.150 --> 00:44:17.583
Yeah, everyone's paranoid,


00:44:17.684 --> 00:44:19.242
'cause they know
if they make one mistake,


00:44:19.353 --> 00:44:21.321
or somebody better comes along,
they're out.


00:44:21.421 --> 00:44:24.083
This isn't a school. It's <i>Survivor.</i>


00:44:24.958 --> 00:44:28.394
Where you guys going? I thought
you were coming with me to Miles'.


00:44:28.495 --> 00:44:29.484
Oh, we'll be back later.


00:44:29.596 --> 00:44:31.860
Franz has to go down to Canal Street
for a defibrillator.


00:44:31.965 --> 00:44:35.230
- Modulator.
- Modulator. And I really need a new hat.


00:44:36.136 --> 00:44:37.194
Ciao.


00:45:04.765 --> 00:45:06.528
That was beautiful.


00:45:07.367 --> 00:45:09.301
Yeah, my man Satie's no joke.


00:45:09.736 --> 00:45:13.194
This place is amazing.
Not exactly struggling.


00:45:13.307 --> 00:45:17.038
Yeah, I consider it a consolation prize
from parents who don't speak.


00:45:18.412 --> 00:45:20.505
Everybody should be here a little later.


00:45:20.614 --> 00:45:23.378
So I figure we should get right
before they start showing up, yeah?


00:45:23.483 --> 00:45:26.452
Look, those beats you gave me?


00:45:26.753 --> 00:45:29.017
They're good. I like them.


00:45:29.890 --> 00:45:33.155
- But they're abstract.
- What do you mean, abstract?


00:45:33.927 --> 00:45:35.622
They're not really danceable.


00:45:36.363 --> 00:45:37.455
Not danceable? What are you...


00:45:37.564 --> 00:45:39.862
You sound like them bubblehead cats
down at the club.


00:45:39.967 --> 00:45:41.901
I'm trying to push it.
That's why I wanted to work with you.


00:45:42.002 --> 00:45:45.335
You want people to like it,
and you want me to dance to it, right?


00:45:45.439 --> 00:45:48.272
- You can't dance to that?
- I can dance to anything.


00:45:48.842 --> 00:45:50.036
But not that?


00:45:51.778 --> 00:45:52.836
Wow.


00:45:53.981 --> 00:45:57.542
All right. All right. So, cool. Tell me
what you want, and I'll work with you.


00:45:57.651 --> 00:46:00.176
- Hey, this was your idea.
- No, it's cool.


00:46:01.221 --> 00:46:03.519
- You sure?
- Yeah, I'm sure.


00:46:04.391 --> 00:46:07.417
Okay. Track four.
Can you make it faster?


00:47:05.252 --> 00:47:07.447
Bloody long trek from that train.


00:47:07.954 --> 00:47:10.514
This is Nigel,
the director I was telling you about.


00:47:10.624 --> 00:47:13.718
It's a pleasure to meet you.
Miles tells me you're a genius.


00:47:13.827 --> 00:47:16.660
Are you sure
he wasn't talking about himself?


00:47:16.763 --> 00:47:18.594
All right, boys. Let's go.


00:47:21.301 --> 00:47:23.633
- What's up, man?
- 50 bucks in Chinatown, baby.


00:47:23.737 --> 00:47:25.136
50 bucks.


00:47:25.972 --> 00:47:28.907
So Nigel thinks we have something hot.


00:47:29.476 --> 00:47:32.104
There's no way I could've done that
without you.


00:47:32.212 --> 00:47:34.646
- It was fun. You were right.
- I know.


00:47:34.748 --> 00:47:36.579
I wish I had more time
to do stuff like that.


00:47:36.683 --> 00:47:39.379
What?
You have all the time in the world.


00:47:39.720 --> 00:47:42.382
Not if I'm going to be
a prima ballerina by 21.


00:47:42.556 --> 00:47:44.820
That's really what you want to do, huh?


00:47:44.925 --> 00:47:46.392
That's the plan.


00:47:47.461 --> 00:47:49.452
Damn. All right.


00:47:49.629 --> 00:47:51.756
I was really hoping that, I don't know...


00:47:52.599 --> 00:47:54.191
me and you could,


00:47:55.836 --> 00:47:57.064
maybe...


00:47:58.205 --> 00:47:59.672
We could what?


00:48:04.511 --> 00:48:06.308
Get a cannoli or something?


00:48:07.714 --> 00:48:10.581
- A cannoli?
- Yeah, a cannoli.


00:48:20.961 --> 00:48:22.861
- I should get some rest.
- Yeah.


00:48:23.163 --> 00:48:25.723
I got my <i>Giselle</i> audition in the morning.


00:48:25.832 --> 00:48:27.129
Yeah, definitely.


00:48:27.868 --> 00:48:29.301
Good night.


00:48:47.554 --> 00:48:50.079
- What part are you auditioning for?
- Giselle.


00:48:51.858 --> 00:48:53.416
Whenever you're ready.


00:49:21.621 --> 00:49:23.851
Yo, Nigel showed me the edits.


00:49:24.291 --> 00:49:26.885
It is coconuts. You rocked it, girl.


00:49:27.494 --> 00:49:29.485
I can't wait to see it.


00:49:31.565 --> 00:49:33.999
- You look beat.
- I am beat.


00:49:34.100 --> 00:49:37.831
Well, give up them feet. It's time for
Dr. Miles' famous foot massage.


00:49:37.938 --> 00:49:40.372
- No, they're awful.
- Oh, no, no, no, no.


00:49:40.474 --> 00:49:42.635
My man Stef got feet
that look like monkey hands,


00:49:42.742 --> 00:49:45.210
so yours can't be that much worse.
Come on.


00:49:45.645 --> 00:49:48.011
- Come on.
- Okay.


00:49:48.348 --> 00:49:50.145
- Oh, my...
- I told you.


00:49:50.250 --> 00:49:51.808
Just playing.


00:49:56.923 --> 00:49:58.288
Feels good, right?


00:50:03.363 --> 00:50:05.263
So why you dancing ballet?


00:50:05.765 --> 00:50:07.062
What do you mean?


00:50:07.267 --> 00:50:12.204
I don't know. It's just so rigid.
You could do so much more.


00:50:14.207 --> 00:50:18.041
Oh, right.
I have the soul of a trombone player.


00:50:18.411 --> 00:50:19.435
Yes.


00:50:22.682 --> 00:50:25.674
I used to dream
about being this classical composer.


00:50:25.785 --> 00:50:28.481
I mean, pounding out notes
on the piano, hour after hour.


00:50:28.588 --> 00:50:30.385
I read every book
written on music theory.


00:50:30.490 --> 00:50:33.015
I wanted to write a symphony
by the time I turned 18.


00:50:33.126 --> 00:50:34.593
What happened?


00:50:34.794 --> 00:50:38.628
Wrote the sketches for my symphony.
Got it into Juilliard and got accepted.


00:50:41.134 --> 00:50:42.829
But you ended up quitting.


00:50:45.005 --> 00:50:46.063
Why?


00:50:50.710 --> 00:50:52.200
Dreams change.


00:50:56.516 --> 00:50:58.211
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!


00:50:58.318 --> 00:51:00.718
- I got the part in the play.
- The quirky brunette?


00:51:00.820 --> 00:51:04.221
- No, the dumb blonde.
- Oh, my God. That's great!


00:51:08.028 --> 00:51:10.895
God, gross.
You're touching her ballerina feet.


00:51:11.598 --> 00:51:13.361
Okay, you know what?
If you guys are going to do that,


00:51:13.466 --> 00:51:15.491
one, wear gloves.


00:51:15.769 --> 00:51:17.396
And two, just...


00:51:22.776 --> 00:51:25.336
<i>How do you know when you're</i>
<i>performing a movement perfectly?</i>


00:51:25.445 --> 00:51:28.471
You feel perfect. You are the
movement.


00:51:29.149 --> 00:51:32.915
Everything is working within you
and through you.


00:51:34.788 --> 00:51:37.052
All effort falls away.


00:51:38.625 --> 00:51:40.593
You disappear into the dance.


00:51:41.828 --> 00:51:45.229
And all that's left
is the purity of the spirit


00:51:46.099 --> 00:51:47.259
and emotion.


00:51:51.237 --> 00:51:52.363
Bella.


00:51:53.206 --> 00:51:55.606
Sara, first line.


00:51:58.612 --> 00:52:00.944
Katrina, could you get the bars please?


00:52:02.182 --> 00:52:03.774
Well, I'd love Giselle.


00:52:03.984 --> 00:52:06.214
I'll be anything
as long as it isn't a peasant.


00:52:06.319 --> 00:52:07.616
I can't stand being a peasant.


00:52:07.721 --> 00:52:09.746
But I'd be happy
with the Queen of the Wilis.


00:52:09.856 --> 00:52:11.949
- Have you ever been a peasant?
- No.


00:52:12.058 --> 00:52:14.652
Well, it's all these
little folksy steps and this...


00:52:16.997 --> 00:52:19.557
I just can't bear it again.


00:52:19.833 --> 00:52:21.528
- Oh, my God.
- There it is.


00:52:26.539 --> 00:52:29.167
Katrina got Giselle.
Well, no surprise there.


00:52:29.609 --> 00:52:32.237
But you got Queen of the Wilis.


00:52:33.113 --> 00:52:35.604
Looks like I'm going to be doing this
for the next six weeks.


00:52:35.715 --> 00:52:37.774
- Okay, see you.
- Oh, where are you going?


00:52:37.884 --> 00:52:39.647
I gotta get to my opening.


00:52:49.496 --> 00:52:51.726
- In a minute. Just a minute.
- Come on.


00:52:52.165 --> 00:52:53.291
In a minute.


00:52:59.039 --> 00:53:01.837
- Look at you.
- What do you think?


00:53:02.676 --> 00:53:04.974
I like it. It's hip.


00:53:05.078 --> 00:53:08.514
- There's a little hop in there, too.
- They're about to start again.


00:53:08.615 --> 00:53:10.242
Come on. Let's go.


00:53:10.350 --> 00:53:11.817
Can't wait to see your new dance piece.


00:53:11.918 --> 00:53:13.943
I need to get some fresh air,
so you guys go ahead.


00:53:14.054 --> 00:53:15.078
- Okay.
- I'll see you inside.


00:53:15.188 --> 00:53:16.416
Be in there.


00:53:29.903 --> 00:53:33.339
You're one of Monique's girls.
Sara, isn't it?


00:53:33.440 --> 00:53:34.805
Yes, that's right.


00:53:34.908 --> 00:53:37.604
Simone Eldaire. I head
the Modern Department at Juilliard.


00:53:37.711 --> 00:53:40.236
I know who you are.
It's an honor to meet you.


00:53:40.346 --> 00:53:42.974
I saw your piece. You were quite good.


00:53:43.683 --> 00:53:46.811
- Who choreographed it?
- I did.


00:53:48.855 --> 00:53:50.186
Congratulations.


00:53:51.491 --> 00:53:52.617
Thank you.


00:53:52.792 --> 00:53:54.783
You've put quite a spell on Monique.


00:53:54.894 --> 00:53:57.556
Whenever I see her,
she just goes on about you.


00:53:57.831 --> 00:53:59.025
Really?


00:54:01.868 --> 00:54:03.358
Our secret.


00:54:03.903 --> 00:54:05.894
I'm down to just one a day.


00:54:06.005 --> 00:54:08.940
Oh, the things we dancers do
to our bodies.


00:54:10.510 --> 00:54:14.207
Ms. Eldaire, if it's okay,
can we just keep this between us?


00:54:14.314 --> 00:54:16.475
- I'm really not supposed to...
- Deal.


00:54:22.489 --> 00:54:25.322
Stop by my office
if you ever want to just talk


00:54:25.425 --> 00:54:28.417
about dance, boys, whatever.


00:54:28.528 --> 00:54:31.361
I know Monique can be a bit severe.


00:54:32.332 --> 00:54:33.697
Thank you. I will.


00:54:34.968 --> 00:54:36.265
It was a pleasure meeting you, Sara.


00:54:36.369 --> 00:54:38.837
I look forward to seeing
more of your work.


00:54:45.245 --> 00:54:46.337
Yes.


00:54:51.985 --> 00:54:55.716
What? Oh, my God!


00:54:55.822 --> 00:54:57.414
Are you kidding me?


00:55:39.499 --> 00:55:42.400
The <i>Vibe</i> is at our party.
Do you know what this means?


00:55:42.502 --> 00:55:44.663
This means... This means exposure.


00:55:44.771 --> 00:55:46.739
This means I'm not gonna
have to spend 25 minutes


00:55:46.840 --> 00:55:50.708
explaining my music to people, they just
gonna hear it and they gonna feel it.


00:55:50.810 --> 00:55:54.177
- I'm so happy for you.
- By me, you mean us, right?


00:55:54.480 --> 00:55:58.610
Miles, this was supposed to be
a one-time deal. I've got school.


00:55:58.718 --> 00:56:00.413
Wow! Right.


00:56:00.620 --> 00:56:02.918
Hey, can't do it, can't do it, right?


00:56:04.958 --> 00:56:08.917
Okay, I've got <i>Giselle</i> rehearsals
four times a week,


00:56:09.028 --> 00:56:13.522
and if I drop Intro to Hip-Hop,
since I get private tutoring anyway,


00:56:14.033 --> 00:56:16.467
- I could do it.
- That would be dope.


00:56:33.686 --> 00:56:36.553
The <i>Vibe</i> guys said
we could have all the time we need.


00:56:39.125 --> 00:56:40.183
Wow.


00:56:40.827 --> 00:56:43.990
- What's all this?
- That is my entire life on tape.


00:56:44.964 --> 00:56:46.989
- How many are there?
- I lost count.


00:56:47.100 --> 00:56:48.965
Over 8,000 hours at least.


00:56:49.636 --> 00:56:50.625
How did you...


00:56:50.737 --> 00:56:53.171
I just always carry around
a tape recorder.


00:56:53.439 --> 00:56:56.033
Started when I was young.
I was just a kid.


00:56:56.709 --> 00:56:59.337
First sound I remember
was the sound of rings jingling


00:56:59.445 --> 00:57:02.471
on the shower-curtain rod
when my mom was giving me a bath.


00:57:02.582 --> 00:57:04.675
- You got a tape of that?
- No. I was four.


00:57:05.184 --> 00:57:06.412
Let me see.


00:57:06.920 --> 00:57:09.047
Let me see. Let me see. Let me see.


00:57:11.724 --> 00:57:12.884
Come on.


00:57:19.832 --> 00:57:21.129
Have a seat.


00:57:30.109 --> 00:57:33.203
- What are we...
- Just listen.


00:57:42.255 --> 00:57:43.586
What is that?


00:57:45.692 --> 00:57:50.425
New York City, East River.
February 27, 1989.


00:57:51.497 --> 00:57:55.797
After five weeks below freezing,
the ice finally breaking.


00:59:55.254 --> 00:59:56.619
Concentrate.


00:59:58.825 --> 01:00:00.258
- You're okay.
- Yeah, I'm all right.


01:00:00.359 --> 01:00:01.917
Watch your turnout.


01:00:03.696 --> 01:00:05.163
Straighten up the line.


01:00:09.969 --> 01:00:11.027
Oh.


01:00:11.237 --> 01:00:14.001
- Katrina.
- You okay?


01:00:14.107 --> 01:00:15.472
- Get away from me. I'm fine.
- You sure?


01:00:15.575 --> 01:00:16.735
- Fine.
- Let's get you up gently.


01:00:16.843 --> 01:00:17.832
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.


01:00:17.944 --> 01:00:20.344
- Can you take her to the clinic, please?
- Sure.


01:00:20.446 --> 01:00:21.470
I'm fine.


01:00:23.316 --> 01:00:26.479
So, in line. Let's go on.


01:00:30.022 --> 01:00:32.547
Bella, and...


01:00:49.342 --> 01:00:51.674
- What?
- Wake up, man.


01:00:52.278 --> 01:00:54.803
Seriously, you've been all
<i>Barney & Friends</i>


01:00:54.914 --> 01:00:57.576
ever since what's-her-name
scrambled your brains.


01:00:57.683 --> 01:01:00.880
- Am not.
- You two are like Bonnie and Clyde,


01:01:01.287 --> 01:01:03.084
Pam and Tommy Lee,


01:01:03.723 --> 01:01:06.191
- Bert and Ernie.
- All right.


01:01:06.292 --> 01:01:08.260
- Lewis and Clark.
- What?


01:01:08.361 --> 01:01:11.524
- Britney and Justin.
- They broke up.


01:01:11.631 --> 01:01:13.997
Seriously, man, you are so hooked.


01:01:14.433 --> 01:01:17.596
It's like watching <i>Bassmasters</i>
on late night cable.


01:01:18.404 --> 01:01:21.100
"And for tackle today,
we're using an eight-pound test line


01:01:21.207 --> 01:01:23.368
"and a blonde ballerina as bait."


01:01:25.311 --> 01:01:27.108
- Get out of here, man.
- You're hooked.


01:01:27.213 --> 01:01:28.680
All right, whatever.


01:01:33.052 --> 01:01:35.418
- You're hooked.
- All right, Eraserhead.


01:01:37.123 --> 01:01:40.456
<i>Hooked</i>
<i>Hooked on</i>


01:01:40.560 --> 01:01:41.618
Oh, that sells.


01:01:41.727 --> 01:01:43.592
The doctor said it was just a sprain.


01:01:43.696 --> 01:01:46.494
The doctor told me
you have permanent ligament damage.


01:01:46.599 --> 01:01:48.191
But Miss Delacroix...


01:01:48.668 --> 01:01:51.034
I'm sorry, Katrina. You can't dance.


01:02:00.846 --> 01:02:02.404
So who gets Giselle?


01:02:08.921 --> 01:02:10.388
It's Sara, isn't it?


01:02:16.829 --> 01:02:20.890
She's making a fool of you.
Ask your son.


01:02:25.471 --> 01:02:27.666
Five, six, seven, eight.


01:02:35.681 --> 01:02:37.842
Yo, stop, stop. Hold up.


01:02:38.985 --> 01:02:42.477
We can't even hear the drums with all
these horns blaring all over the place!


01:02:42.588 --> 01:02:44.385
Okay. You know what?
I'm really sick and tired of all your...


01:02:44.490 --> 01:02:46.720
Hey, why don't we just take a break?


01:02:48.728 --> 01:02:51.629
I really don't know, man.
Who does she think she is?


01:02:56.135 --> 01:02:58.797
- What?
- You're amazing.


01:03:01.173 --> 01:03:02.470
So are you.


01:03:05.811 --> 01:03:08.245
There's something I need to talk to you
about, actually...


01:03:08.347 --> 01:03:10.907
Can we not take so many breaks
here today?


01:03:11.017 --> 01:03:12.609
Some of us have a life.


01:03:17.957 --> 01:03:19.083
What is it?


01:03:21.827 --> 01:03:22.987
It's nothing.


01:03:24.897 --> 01:03:27.229
All right, let's take it from the top.


01:03:27.333 --> 01:03:29.631
Five, six, seven, eight.


01:03:43.749 --> 01:03:46.513
- You really did a job this time.
- This has nothing to do with you.


01:03:46.619 --> 01:03:49.019
You're right.
It has everything to do with her.


01:03:49.121 --> 01:03:51.146
Jesus, you don't care about her!


01:03:51.257 --> 01:03:52.952
- You need her...
- She's gifted...


01:03:53.059 --> 01:03:55.289
...more than she needs you.
...the way you were.


01:03:55.394 --> 01:03:57.988
- But you threw yours away.
- Please.


01:03:58.097 --> 01:04:00.691
For what? So some kids
on the street could know your name.


01:04:00.800 --> 01:04:03.064
My dream changed. That's all.


01:04:03.169 --> 01:04:05.763
I think you're just ashamed of
where you come from.


01:04:05.871 --> 01:04:09.102
No. I'm ashamed that you can't accept
that my history is out there


01:04:09.208 --> 01:04:11.233
and not inside this
white marble mausoleum.


01:04:11.344 --> 01:04:13.312
- You sound like your father.
- Fancy that.


01:04:13.412 --> 01:04:15.573
You're angry at me, be angry at me.
But let her alone.


01:04:15.681 --> 01:04:16.773
I love her.


01:04:24.824 --> 01:04:25.882
Well, good.


01:04:27.326 --> 01:04:28.953
Let her live her dream.


01:04:29.795 --> 01:04:31.558
Don't destroy hers, as well.


01:04:46.045 --> 01:04:48.036
So just remember...


01:04:48.147 --> 01:04:49.512
- Sara.
- Yes?


01:04:49.615 --> 01:04:52.607
Could you do me a favor and get me
my notes from the last design meeting?


01:04:52.718 --> 01:04:54.015
They're on my desk.


01:04:54.120 --> 01:04:55.883
- Sure.
- Bye.


01:05:30.823 --> 01:05:32.620
Sara, I...


01:05:34.894 --> 01:05:39.831
I tried. I tried to tell you in the park,
in rehearsal...


01:05:41.801 --> 01:05:44.964
I wanted to tell you.
I just didn't know how to step to you.


01:05:45.070 --> 01:05:46.628
I still don't.


01:05:47.106 --> 01:05:48.573
I was afraid I'd lose you.


01:05:48.674 --> 01:05:52.508
And I knew if it came down to me
or ballet, you'd choose ballet.


01:05:54.547 --> 01:05:56.515
- I love you...
- Don't say that.


01:05:59.752 --> 01:06:01.185
I believed you.


01:06:03.489 --> 01:06:07.220
I believed that someone who can
create music as beautifully as you


01:06:07.326 --> 01:06:09.624
had to be telling the truth.


01:06:17.803 --> 01:06:21.762
You know what, Miles?
You're just another player.


01:06:29.582 --> 01:06:34.110
Yes, I know Miles was a total jerk, but...


01:06:34.220 --> 01:06:38.589
You know, it's not like his mother
is a freaking saint, either.


01:06:39.425 --> 01:06:42.451
Okay.
This happens to me way too much.


01:06:42.561 --> 01:06:44.392
I'm a dumb blonde.


01:06:44.763 --> 01:06:46.094
I'm gonna go now.


01:06:50.736 --> 01:06:51.964
Sara.


01:06:52.872 --> 01:06:54.703
I want you to dance Giselle.


01:06:58.711 --> 01:07:00.269
Everything all right?


01:07:01.780 --> 01:07:04.476
- I feel like such an idiot.
- Don't.


01:07:04.583 --> 01:07:08.178
Miles has never cared what effect
his actions have on other people.


01:07:08.287 --> 01:07:10.278
I've arranged for you to be moved
to a single room,


01:07:10.389 --> 01:07:12.118
so you can concentrate
on your preparation.


01:07:12.224 --> 01:07:15.250
- I don't need to.
- You need to rest. Get some sleep.


01:08:56.495 --> 01:08:59.555
Stop! Paul, just cut it out!


01:08:59.898 --> 01:09:01.627
You know you're not supposed
to stick out.


01:09:01.734 --> 01:09:03.827
You're supposed to blend.
You're a peasant.


01:09:03.936 --> 01:09:05.403
I'm coming up there.


01:09:06.605 --> 01:09:09.665
Sara. Hey, Miles doesn't know
I'm telling you this so...


01:09:09.775 --> 01:09:11.140
And he'd probably beat me up
if he found out,


01:09:11.243 --> 01:09:12.369
so, please don't tell him, okay?


01:09:12.478 --> 01:09:14.309
- Okay.
- He needs you.


01:09:14.413 --> 01:09:15.812
The dancers won't listen to him,


01:09:15.914 --> 01:09:17.381
everything's falling apart.
Luckily, the guys...


01:09:17.483 --> 01:09:20.384
I can't do anything, okay. I have <i>Giselle.</i>


01:09:21.520 --> 01:09:22.714
I'm sorry.


01:09:23.989 --> 01:09:25.479
Okay, fine. That's cool.


01:09:25.591 --> 01:09:27.752
No. No, that's not cool.


01:09:27.860 --> 01:09:29.293
Look, whatever happened
between you and Miles


01:09:29.395 --> 01:09:30.794
doesn't mean you can't help out.


01:09:30.896 --> 01:09:33.057
- You just don't want to.
- That's not fair.


01:09:33.165 --> 01:09:37.363
You're like mini-Monique. Jeté, jeté.


01:09:37.469 --> 01:09:41.030
- Zoe.
- I feel like I swallowed a bug.


01:09:45.678 --> 01:09:47.669
Sara, we can't come to your ballet.


01:09:47.780 --> 01:09:49.042
It's not 'cause of Zoe or anything,


01:09:49.148 --> 01:09:51.981
it's just we have dress rehearsal
that night and...


01:09:52.117 --> 01:09:54.585
Well, we need all the rehearsal
we can get.


01:09:55.487 --> 01:09:56.715
Sorry.


01:09:57.790 --> 01:09:59.087
I understand.


01:10:07.399 --> 01:10:09.765
Sara, can you come up on stage,
please?


01:10:09.868 --> 01:10:10.926
Yes.


01:10:22.948 --> 01:10:24.575
Watch that rouge.


01:10:26.452 --> 01:10:27.646
Ta-da!


01:10:29.188 --> 01:10:31.782
- Isn't it lovely?
- What's it for?


01:10:34.259 --> 01:10:37.524
I'm having a dinner party
after the performance at my home.


01:10:38.530 --> 01:10:40.464
Absolutely everyone will be there,


01:10:40.566 --> 01:10:43.763
even the Chairman of the board
of American Ballet Theatre.


01:10:45.304 --> 01:10:46.601
Are you pleased?


01:10:52.711 --> 01:10:56.147
- Are you nervous?
- Yes.


01:10:56.248 --> 01:10:59.411
You shouldn't be. You're my student.


01:10:59.785 --> 01:11:04.154
Now remember to watch
those extensions and think up.


01:11:04.790 --> 01:11:05.757
<i>Merde.</i>


01:11:19.805 --> 01:11:20.772
Excuse me, you can't go...


01:11:20.873 --> 01:11:24.070
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I know her.
Thank you.


01:11:25.511 --> 01:11:28.071
- Wow, look at you.
- Hey, okay, no, no, no.


01:11:28.180 --> 01:11:31.206
Don't be nice yet, okay?


01:11:31.350 --> 01:11:33.818
There are two things. No.


01:11:38.524 --> 01:11:43.154
"I just wanted to say that I'm sorry


01:11:43.262 --> 01:11:44.593
"and that I love you so much.


01:11:44.696 --> 01:11:47.722
"Because no matter how stupid or crazy
I act, you've always been there for me.


01:11:47.833 --> 01:11:51.030
"And I'm sorry. Break a leg. Love, Zoe."


01:11:52.638 --> 01:11:55.698
- It's okay.
- No, no, no, it's not okay,


01:11:55.808 --> 01:11:58.470
'cause I was such a bitch and...


01:11:58.577 --> 01:12:00.738
God, I am so proud of you, Sara.


01:12:00.946 --> 01:12:05.110
You did it. You know, you did
what you said you were going to do.


01:12:05.884 --> 01:12:09.149
- You're so rad.
- You're the rad one.


01:12:09.421 --> 01:12:12.356
- And so blonde.
- I know.


01:12:13.625 --> 01:12:16.253
I kind of like being a dumb blonde.


01:12:17.229 --> 01:12:19.459
You know I think Franz likes it, too.


01:12:19.565 --> 01:12:21.055
Men are so easy.


01:12:21.366 --> 01:12:24.392
<i>Fifteen minutes to places, please.</i>
<i>Fifteen minutes.</i>


01:12:25.003 --> 01:12:29.167
You have some twirling to do.
I'm gonna try and not whistle too loud.


01:12:29.274 --> 01:12:31.174
Wait. You said two things.


01:12:31.610 --> 01:12:33.100
Please don't hate me.


01:12:33.312 --> 01:12:36.304
I nearly killed Franz
when he asked me to do this.


01:12:38.417 --> 01:12:40.146
It's from Miles.


01:17:08.920 --> 01:17:10.717
Wonderful!


01:17:12.891 --> 01:17:14.654
Giselle!


01:17:49.494 --> 01:17:51.428
Oh, great job.


01:17:51.530 --> 01:17:53.623
- It was great. It was wonderful.
- Good, good, good, thank you.


01:18:07.179 --> 01:18:09.545
Sara, there you are.


01:18:11.016 --> 01:18:13.280
What on earth are you doing here?


01:18:14.085 --> 01:18:16.417
Everyone wants to congratulate you.


01:18:21.726 --> 01:18:23.091
What's the matter?


01:18:24.162 --> 01:18:25.595
Is something wrong?


01:18:29.100 --> 01:18:31.227
Oh, you must be exhausted.


01:18:31.903 --> 01:18:35.066
I can remember coming off stage
after a performance,


01:18:35.173 --> 01:18:37.073
barely able to walk.


01:18:38.643 --> 01:18:40.702
You leave everything on the stage.


01:18:42.347 --> 01:18:44.474
It's the best feeling in the world.


01:18:49.254 --> 01:18:53.122
- Did you ever wonder if...
- What?


01:18:54.826 --> 01:18:58.421
- If it was enough?
- Enough?


01:19:01.299 --> 01:19:05.463
Dear girl, once you get a taste for it,
it's never enough.


01:19:05.804 --> 01:19:08.773
In time, there are better sets,
lovelier costumes...


01:19:08.873 --> 01:19:09.965
No.


01:19:11.209 --> 01:19:15.737
Did you ever wonder
if this was all you'd ever do,


01:19:15.847 --> 01:19:17.405
all you'd ever be?


01:19:17.649 --> 01:19:20.277
Let's go. Everyone's waiting.


01:19:20.652 --> 01:19:24.452
Miss Delacroix, I don't think
I want to be just a ballerina.


01:19:24.556 --> 01:19:26.922
- It's just nerves.
- You're not listening.


01:19:27.559 --> 01:19:30.027
I can't give up everything for ballet.


01:19:30.128 --> 01:19:31.755
No one's asking you
to give up everything.


01:19:31.863 --> 01:19:33.194
But you will.


01:19:33.598 --> 01:19:37.364
Maybe not on purpose,
maybe not all at once.


01:19:41.406 --> 01:19:45.308
Listen to me, Sara,
there are hundreds of thousands of girls


01:19:45.410 --> 01:19:47.605
who would kill to be in your position.


01:19:47.712 --> 01:19:52.445
Your gift means nothing
without hard work, discipline


01:19:53.184 --> 01:19:56.244
and yes, sacrifice.


01:19:57.055 --> 01:19:59.751
You just have a child's idea
of happiness.


01:20:01.026 --> 01:20:04.154
And to be great you have to...
You have to let that go.


01:20:06.498 --> 01:20:07.795
Why?


01:20:10.335 --> 01:20:12.235
I'll wait for you in the limo.


01:20:12.837 --> 01:20:15.271
I'm sorry. I can't go to your party.


01:20:34.693 --> 01:20:37.184
- You changed the song again!
- I had to.


01:20:37.295 --> 01:20:40.492
And I'm just supposed to redo
all the steps?


01:20:40.632 --> 01:20:42.463
This is your mess, you fix it.


01:20:42.567 --> 01:20:44.501
- Candy, please.
- No.


01:20:44.602 --> 01:20:47.833
You holler when you sort it all out,
Mr. Control Freak!


01:20:47.939 --> 01:20:50.669
You know the number,
unless you changed that, too.


01:20:53.745 --> 01:20:57.044
Miles, what are we gonna do now?


01:20:57.982 --> 01:21:00.610
I don't know, man.
Just give me a minute.


01:21:13.965 --> 01:21:17.992
- Sara, I...
- No, don't say anything.


01:21:20.238 --> 01:21:21.671
Please just listen.


01:21:22.540 --> 01:21:25.373
I danced the best
I've ever danced tonight.


01:21:26.378 --> 01:21:28.243
It was close to perfect.


01:21:29.447 --> 01:21:32.712
When I was done, I closed my eyes


01:21:32.817 --> 01:21:35.251
and I felt such peace.


01:21:36.421 --> 01:21:38.116
But when I opened them,


01:21:39.424 --> 01:21:43.292
everyone was standing and clapping.


01:21:45.930 --> 01:21:48.296
And I felt nothing.


01:21:51.903 --> 01:21:53.200
Just numb.


01:21:54.939 --> 01:21:58.705
And I thought to myself,
"That's an odd thing to feel.


01:21:59.043 --> 01:22:02.444
"I've worked my whole life
to get to this place,


01:22:03.014 --> 01:22:04.914
"and I feel nothing?"


01:22:06.985 --> 01:22:09.476
And then there you were.


01:22:11.389 --> 01:22:13.482
You popped into my head.


01:22:14.292 --> 01:22:16.624
I couldn't stop thinking about you.


01:22:18.096 --> 01:22:22.590
Your face, your smile,
and what you said that day in class.


01:22:23.668 --> 01:22:25.397
"I am here."


01:22:34.913 --> 01:22:39.612
And I realized this whole time, I've been
trying to perfect someone else's steps


01:22:39.751 --> 01:22:41.844
instead of finding my own.


01:22:43.588 --> 01:22:45.681
Well, I wanna be here, too.


01:22:47.091 --> 01:22:50.458
I wanna paint with ballerinas, b-boys


01:22:50.562 --> 01:22:52.757
in point shoes and high-tops.


01:22:54.098 --> 01:22:57.226
If my dream of dancing ballet


01:22:57.335 --> 01:22:59.599
doesn't have enough room for all that,


01:22:59.704 --> 01:23:02.969
my friends,
and you with a cannoli once in a while,


01:23:04.943 --> 01:23:08.208
then I'm gonna have to find a dream
big enough that does.


01:23:10.048 --> 01:23:12.915
And all I was gonna say was,
"I'm sorry."


01:23:25.463 --> 01:23:28.591
So, looks like you're having
some trouble with your dancers.


01:23:28.700 --> 01:23:32.966
Yeah. We got 24 hours to get right,
and we looking kind of wrong right now.


01:23:33.071 --> 01:23:34.766
You know what I'm saying?


01:23:37.408 --> 01:23:38.841
You want some help?


01:23:43.014 --> 01:23:45.244
You're not gonna make me beg,
are you?


01:23:47.919 --> 01:23:51.514
Miles, please let me help you.


01:23:54.192 --> 01:23:55.352
All right.


01:27:38.316 --> 01:27:39.283
<i>I'm out.</i>

